---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Partners — Army Pink" description="Army Pink partners with wellness providers, yoga studios, and community organizations to give survivors access to healing resources they couldn't access alone.">

  <!-- PAGE HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="pill-label reveal-item">Our Partners</span>
    <h1 class="reveal-item">Healing happens<br>together.</h1>
    <p class="reveal-item">
      Army Pink doesn't build everything ourselves — we build bridges.
      Our partners bring clinical expertise, wellness programming, and community
      reach that survivors couldn't access on their own.
    </p>
    <div class="page-hero-actions reveal-item">
      <a href="#become-a-partner" class="btn btn-primary">Become a partner</a>
      <a href="#current-partners" class="btn btn-ghost">See our partners</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PHILOSOPHY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="pill-label reveal-item">Our Approach</span>
        <h2 class="reveal-item" style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
          Partners, not sponsors.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-block reveal-item">
        <p>"This program is made possible by..." — not "brought to you by."</p>
        <cite>Army Pink's partnership philosophy, modeled on the PBS/NPR approach to supporter recognition.</cite>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-grid" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
        <div class="prose-text reveal-item">
          <h2>Survivor spaces stay sacred.</h2>
          <p>
            We keep a clear separation between where survivors heal and where partners
            receive recognition. In crisis and healing spaces — the Calm Room, the
            Escape Club's support channels, safety planning tools — the experience is
            entirely about the survivor.
          </p>
          <p>
            Partner visibility lives in public-facing content, annual reports, and
            impact dashboards. Funders get meaningful attribution. Survivors get
            undistracted support.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-text reveal-item">
          <h2>Impact-centered attribution.</h2>
          <p>
            We don't put logos on safety tools. Instead, we tell the real story:
            "Thanks to Vedanta Wellness Studio, 47 survivors accessed free
            trauma-informed yoga this quarter."
          </p>
          <p>
            That kind of attribution is more meaningful to funders — and completely
            safe for survivors. Partners become part of the mission story, not a
            banner above it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FEATURED PARTNER: VEDANTA -->
  <section class="section" id="current-partners" style="background: var(--beige);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="pill-label reveal-item">Featured Partner</span>
        <h2 class="reveal-item" style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
          Made possible by our partners.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="partner-featured-card reveal-item">
        <div>
          <span class="partner-type">Wellness Partner</span>
          <h3>Vedanta Wellness Studio</h3>
          <p>
            Vedanta brings trauma-informed yoga and meditation programming directly
            into Army Pink's Calm Room. Their instructors understand the
            specific experience of domestic violence survivors — no pressure, no
            performance, just gentle movement and nervous system support.
          </p>
          <p>
            Together, we're co-creating the <strong>Pathway to Wellness</strong>
            program — a structured healing journey from escape to embodiment,
            designed specifically for DV survivors and grant-funded for free access.
          </p>
          <a href="/wellness-portal" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: var(--space-sm); display: inline-flex;">
            Explore the Calm Room
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-featured-image">
          <img src="/img/empowering-hero.jpg" alt="Vedanta wellness partnership" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Additional partner slots -->
      <div class="partner-grid">
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item">
          <span class="partner-type">Technology Partner</span>
          <h4>Do Yoga With Me</h4>
          <p>
            Providing curated yoga and meditation content through our Calm Room —
            from sleep aids and breathwork to full programs for managing anxiety
            and life transitions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item" style="border-style: dashed; background: transparent;">
          <span class="partner-type">Coming Soon</span>
          <h4>Transportation Partner</h4>
          <p>
            We're actively seeking rideshare and transportation partners to power
            Freedom Rides. If your organization can help move survivors safely,
            we want to talk.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item" style="border-style: dashed; background: transparent;">
          <span class="partner-type">Coming Soon</span>
          <h4>Corporate Sponsor</h4>
          <p>
            Champion-level corporate partners fund free survivor access and receive
            named recognition in our impact reports and annual gala. Inquire below.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PARTNERSHIP MODELS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="pill-label reveal-item">Partnership Models</span>
        <h2 class="reveal-item" style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
          Ways to partner with us.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="partner-grid">
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item">
          <span class="partner-type">Model A</span>
          <h4>Subsidized Access</h4>
          <p>
            Provide free or reduced-cost services to Army Pink survivors.
            We handle outreach and matching; you provide the expertise.
            Great for wellness providers, therapists, and service organizations.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item">
          <span class="partner-type">Model B</span>
          <h4>Embedded Content</h4>
          <p>
            Your content — guided meditations, yoga classes, courses — embedded
            directly in our Calm Room. Survivors access it through us;
            partners gain mission-aligned exposure.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item">
          <span class="partner-type">Model C</span>
          <h4>Co-Created Program</h4>
          <p>
            Joint programming designed from scratch for DV survivors.
            The deepest impact model, and the most fundable for grants.
            Currently active with Vedanta.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-card reveal-item">
          <span class="partner-type">Model D</span>
          <h4>Corporate Sponsorship</h4>
          <p>
            Fund survivor access at scale. Named recognition in reports, events,
            and the annual impact dashboard. Tax-deductible through our fiscal
            sponsor, Charity On Top.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="cta-section" id="become-a-partner">
    <h2 class="reveal-item">Interested in partnering?</h2>
    <p class="reveal-item">
      Whether you're a wellness provider, a corporation, or a community organization —
      if you want to put your resources behind survivor healing, let's talk.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-actions reveal-item">
      <a href="mailto:wei@weiyandesign.com" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
      <a href="/mission" class="btn btn-ghost">Learn about our mission</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</Layout>
